{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner, on hugh word at 20:37 that other tasks may go to the cloud through this sprint, launched three sessions at 20:40 Eastern from planner/i5-demo-host 13ae3055. (1) Issues and a verify summary (session_015zxJDX2MsVMPqsMns5JBSP): artroom issue open, comment, assign, close and issues through the issue lane existing acts and the demo profile; artroom edit and merge gain --closes so the publishing merge closes the issue as the lane scenario does; artroom verify --all prints one line per scope and a last line, the demo script shot 12. (2) Pin before install (session_01MJtubujy2VKjeApUrXwmRr): the register id is a pure function of the install seed, so artroom install --plan prints the id and saves the seed, the operator sets the host setting, then artroom install --planned founds with that seed; and a scope object resends a recorded unsent attempt on the next turn once the outside port accepts its kind, exactly once, so the old order no longer waits for a restart. (3) The story page (session_01GqVH3LjdgG7zFbLE2ZDHMX): request/i5-page merged forward onto the demo base, served from the scope Worker at /page/, signed in with a key and a membership session, issues and changes with their refusals by name, the one-file manifest and the rendered page link, the acts the member may do now; screenshots if the container browser works. Builder reads, gates, files and lands each after the branches already filed; the planner runs them live.","body":{"base":"planner/i5-demo-host@13ae3055","sessions":"3"}}